# Develop a plugin command

Read [AGENTS.md](../../../AGENTS.md), especially command development and the
public API contract. Use this workflow for a new leaf or changed command.

1. Inspect `Get-PluginCommandDefinitionList`, `Get-PluginMenuHandler` and
   `Get-PluginHelloHandler`; identify direct and menu routes under `{{Namespace}}`.
2. Define observable success, invalid arguments, Escape and failure outcomes.
   Add source-mirrored tests using the supplied API fixture; run
   `Invoke-NovaTest` and confirm the intended changed-behavior failure.
3. Add the cohesive handler factory, capture `$Gerber` with `.GetNewClosure()`,
   register the leaf and wire the parent's action table and dispatch.
4. Extend the built-module public integration test to execute the handler and
   verify manifest identity. Run `Invoke-NovaBuild`, `Invoke-NovaTest` and
   `Test-NovaBuild`; preserve the coverage gate.
5. Update README and Unreleased changelog, run analyzer/CodeScene checks as
   described in AGENTS.md and report evidence. Only when authorized, use an
   isolated local publication and fresh Gerber host to verify the actual slash
   command. Do not equate registration with installation.
